{"finding":{"specification":"SSLContextSpec","message":"the TrustManager[] given to SSLContext.init holds a manager of a class the application defines and was not observed coming from a TrustManagerFactory","class":"org.cryptomator.data.cloud.webdav.network.SSLSocketFactories","method":"from","joint_findings":[],"detector":{"tool":"rvsec","kind":"runtime_monitor"}},"confirmed_cause":"The `trustManager` parameter reaches `SSLContext.init` as `arrayOf<TrustManager>(trustManager)`. Its resolved WebDAV callers supply application-defined `DefaultTrustManager` or `PinningTrustManager`, not a TrustManagerFactory-produced manager array. Although DefaultTrustManager internally delegates to a factory-produced manager, the object passed to `init` is the wrapper; PinningTrustManager is directly constructed and enforces certificate-pin and hostname checks. Therefore `generatedTrustManagers[tm]` is violated for the reported TrustManager[] argument (CLM-001, CLM-003, CLM-004).","plan_invariants":["The governed SSLContext.init call receives a TrustManager[] produced by a TrustManagerFactory initialized with a null KeyStore, rather than an array containing an application-defined manager (CLM-001, CLM-003).","The TLS selector remains TLSv1.3 on Android Q and later and TLSv1.2 on earlier Android versions; this selector does not itself define enabled or negotiated handshake protocols (CLM-002, CLM-005).","The existing null KeyManager[] and null SecureRandom SSLContext.init arguments remain unchanged because they are separate, unreported predicates.","WebDavCompatibleHttpClient continues to select and retain its existing DefaultTrustManager or PinningTrustManager configuration outside SSLSocketFactories.from; PinningTrustManager's existing certificate-pin hostname verifier is not replaced, removed, or broadened (CLM-003, CLM-004).","The pinning route must continue to reject a host whose peer certificate does not have the configured pin (CLM-004).","No stored value, exported value, persisted-object format, or cloud-content payload format is changed.","No unit-test edit is planned: this change replaces the platform trust-manager source used by TLS setup, and its observable effect is provider/network handshake behavior rather than a repository-owned branch or parsed value that the available unit-test classpath can exercise."],"plan_forbidden_changes":["Do not replace, weaken, or remove the existing PinningTrustManager certificate-pin or hostname-verification configuration in WebDavCompatibleHttpClient.","Do not accept more certificates or host names than the existing DefaultTrustManager and PinningTrustManager routes accept.","Do not change or pin the TLS protocol selector; retain TLSv1.3 on Android Q and later and TLSv1.2 on earlier Android versions.","Do not alter the null KeyManager[] or SecureRandom arguments, which are separate unreported SSLContextSpec predicates.","Do not rename SSLSocketFactories.from.","Do not edit DefaultTrustManager.kt or PinningTrustManager.kt because their exact source is unavailable in the manifest.","Do not edit unrelated cloud persistence, export, or stored-value-format paths."],"parameter_policies":[],"adjudication_concerns":[{"kind":"Any patch replacing the pinning trust manager with a factory-created manager must preserve the currently enforced certificate-pin and hostname acceptance policy.","description":"Builds, unit tests, and source rechecks cannot decide whether a replacement continues to trust exactly the intended peer certificates and host names. Human review would need to authorize and verify any changed trust policy."},{"kind":"The case policy forbids a change that accepts more certificates or host names, but a rule-compliant replacement for the PinningTrustManager route has not been established that preserves its certificate-pin and hostname checks.","description":"Generating a rule-only replacement would require authorizing a changed trust policy despite the stated policy condition. A reviewer would hav